Taken from Jellyfin's FFmpeg (jellyfin-ffmpeg, debian/patches/0086-fix-amd-hevc-vaapi-encoder-extradata-with-overrides.patch),
its muxer part, GPL like the rest of this build, with thanks to its authors.
An HEVC stream labelled hvc1 lost the descriptions of its pictures that
the encoder writes before each key picture, leaving only the one at the
head of the file. AMD's encoder works with settings that description does
not quite give, and a browser decoded the key pictures and broke up every
picture between them into blocks: seen on an RX 6600, H.264 from the same
card playing right. Kept in the stream, the encoder's own description is
the one a reader goes by.

--- a/libavformat/movenc.c
+++ b/libavformat/movenc.c
@@ -7110,7 +7110,9 @@
     } else if (par->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC && trk->extradata_size[trk->last_stsd_index] > 6 &&
                (AV_RB24(trk->extradata[trk->last_stsd_index]) == 1 || AV_RB32(trk->extradata[trk->last_stsd_index]) == 1)) {
         /* extradata is Annex B, assume the bitstream is too and convert it */
-        int filter_ps = (trk->tag == MKTAG('h','v','c','1'));
+        /* Kept in the stream whatever the tag: a reader trusts them over
+         * the sample entry, which may not describe what was encoded. */
+        int filter_ps = 0;
         if (trk->hint_track >= 0 && trk->hint_track < mov->nb_tracks) {
             ret = ff_hevc_annexb2mp4_buf(pkt->data, &reformatted_data,
                                          &size, filter_ps, NULL);
